TITLE:: RLAutomorphism
summary:: A way of moving every object of a relation context that its relations go through: a complete isography
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLNetwork, Classes/RLRelationContext, Classes/RLCategory, Classes/RLMorphism, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
An automorphism of an link::Classes/RLRelationContext:: is a one-to-one map strong::nu:: of its objects together with the change it makes to the relations: a relation m becomes N(m), "move back, do m, move forth", so that code::nu(m(x)) = N(m)(nu(x))::. It is strong::valid:: when every N(m) is again one of the relations the context generates (link::#-isValid::).

Applied to a network (link::Classes/RLNetwork#-transformedBy::) it moves the contents by nu and the labels by N: the network keeps its shape and its sense. Applied again and again to a small network it makes a sequence: Popoff's "composing with automorphisms".

Three families to know:

list::
## strong::T and I on pitch classes:: (code::RLRelationContext.pitchClasses::): the maps x -> kx + c with k prime to the number of steps (link::#*affine::). In 12 steps there are 48; they realise 24 of the 48 automorphisms of the group, those Klumpenhouwer's isographies call <T(p)>, <I(p)> with p even, and their multiplicative cousins. The others exist only node by node (link::Classes/RLNetwork#-localIsographies::). In 19 steps all 342 are realised.
## strong::chords under P, L, R:: (code::RLRelationContext.triads::): transpositions and inversions change no label; maps that treat major and minor chords differently change them (Gesualdo's "majors a fifth up, minors in place" sends L to R and R to RLR).
## strong::Cube Dance:: (code::RLRelationContext.cubeDance::): 7776 automorphisms after Popoff, over the 12 automorphisms of the monoid of U, P, L. Transpositions and inversions change no label; so does moving one hexatonic system alone by a major third; others send U to PUP.
::

code::
~cd = RLRelationContext.cubeDance;
~sp = ~cd.space;
~t5 = RLAutomorphism.transposition(~cd, 5);
[~t5.isValid, ~t5.order];                                   // [true, 12]
~t5.onArrow(\U) == ~cd.transform(\U);                       // true

~cell = RLNetwork.chain(~cd, [~sp.major(2), ~sp.chord(2, \aug), ~sp.minor(7)], [\U, \U]);
~cell.iterate(~t5, 11).collect(_.objects).flat;             // 36 chords: every step one voice up a semitone

~pcs = RLRelationContext.pitchClasses;
~m = RLAutomorphism.affine(~pcs, 5, 2);                     // x -> 5x + 2
~pcs.nameOf(~m.onArrow(\I3));                               // I7
~pcs.category.automorphisms.includesEqual(~m.arrowMap);     // true: one of the 48

RLAutomorphism(~cd, [[~sp.major(0), ~sp.major(1)], [~sp.major(1), ~sp.major(0)]]).isValid;   // false
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: context
An link::Classes/RLRelationContext::.
argument:: rule
A Function object -> object, or an Array of code::[object, image]:: pairs (objects left out stay in place). A map that is not one to one, or that leaves the context's objects, is an Error.
argument:: label

METHOD:: transposition
Chords moved by their roots: every root up by v. For contexts of chords of an RLEDO.

METHOD:: inversion
Every pitch class x of every chord turned into k - x.

METHOD:: affine
On pitch classes: x -> kx + c.

METHOD:: all
METHOD:: count
Every automorphism of a context, and their number: for each automorphism N of its monoid (or for those given as code::arrowMaps::, as link::Classes/RLCategory#-automorphisms:: lists them), the one-to-one maps of the objects that turn each generator g into N(g). The images are tried object by object and a choice kept only while every pair already placed agrees; nil past code::max::.
code::
RLAutomorphism.count(RLRelationContext.pitchClasses(RLEDO(12)));     // 48: the maps x -> kx + c
RLAutomorphism.count(RLRelationContext.cubeDance);                   // 7776 (some seconds): 648 for each of 12
RLAutomorphism.all(RLRelationContext.pitchClasses(RLEDO(12))).first; // an RLAutomorphism
::

METHOD:: extend
From a few objects and their images, the rest filled by what the invertible relations force: code::nu(m(x)) = N(m)(nu(x)):: for every relation m that can be undone.
argument:: context
argument:: seeds
code::[[object, image], ...]::, one per orbit of the invertible relations. Objects not reached stay in place.
argument:: arrowMap
How the relations change: one of code::context.category.automorphisms::; nil for "not at all".
argument:: label

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: context
METHOD:: images
The images of the context's objects, in their order.
METHOD:: label

METHOD:: value
The image of an object. code::automorphism.(x)::.

METHOD:: onArrow
What a relation (given as an arrow, a name or a word) becomes.

METHOD:: isValid
Whether every generator becomes one of the context's relations.

METHOD:: arrowMap
How it moves the arrows of the context's category, as an Array of indices comparable with those of link::Classes/RLCategory#-automorphisms::; nil when it is not valid.

METHOD:: <>
This after that.

METHOD:: inverse
METHOD:: repeated
METHOD:: order
Undone; n times; how many times before everything is back in place.

METHOD:: isIdentity
